    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490-a2">

                <pb facs="0627" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg585"/>

                <head>[Extract.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. M. S. Phaeton</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Barbadoes</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 7, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>“I have to inform you that the paddle-wheel steamer Dolphin, of Liverpool, which
                    left St. Thomas for Nassau at midnight of the 24th March, was captured by the
                    Wachusett, twenty-five miles to the leeward of that island.</p>
                <p>“The Wachusett returned to St. Thomas with the crew of the Dolphin, and these
                    sixteen persons presented themselves at the British consulate on the 27th.”</p>
            </div>
        </body>
